<div class="hero">
  <div class="lft">
    <h1>A brain that wires up <em>honest software</em>.</h1>
    <p class="lede">NeuroTrocity is what happens when a brain fires every idea at once — thousands of them, all shouting, each one certain it's the billion-dollar one. Most are noise. The few that survive get built properly, and become ventures.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn p" href="#ventures">Meet the ventures <span class="arw">→</span></a>
      <a class="btn g" href="#ethos">How we work</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="rgt"></div>
  <canvas id="cortex"></canvas>
  <div class="feather"></div>
</div>

<div class="stats">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="stat"><div class="n">Ventures</div><div class="l">Shipping &amp; growing</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="n"><b>1</b> rule</div><div class="l">Behave</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="n"><b>∞</b> ideas</div><div class="l">Firing all at once</div></div>
  </div>
</div>

<section id="ventures">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rule"><span>The ventures</span><i></i></div>
    <h2 class="reveal-h">Every venture, one rule: behave.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Each venture is its own complete product — built to do one thing properly, then get out of your way. More are on the way.</p>
    <div class="man">
      <a class="vrow" href="/dosetrack/landing/" style="--c:var(--dose)"><span class="sl">/dosetrack</span><span class="ds">Medication reminders that actually stick — free for your first five meds, forever.</span><span class="mt">iPhone · Watch</span><span class="go">→</span></a>
      <a class="vrow" href="/dispoint/landing/" style="--c:var(--dis)"><span class="sl">/dispoint</span><span class="ds">Deals and bonus-points offers, sorted by what's about to expire.</span><span class="mt">iPhone · AU</span><span class="go">→</span></a>
      <a class="vrow" href="/rewire/landing/" style="--c:var(--rw)"><span class="sl">/rewire</span><span class="ds">Underperforming business websites, rebuilt so they actually work.</span><span class="mt">Web · AU</span><span class="go">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="ethos" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rule"><span>How we work</span><i></i></div>
    <h2 class="reveal-h">Four rules. No exceptions.</h2>
    <div class="runin">
      <div><b>Sharp, not sprawling.</b> One thing, done properly. No feature bloat, no roadmap theatre, no app that grows until it's miserable to use.</div>
      <div><b>Honest by default.</b> No manipulative nudges, no engineered regret. If a choice is good for us and bad for you, we don't ship it.</div>
      <div><b>Your data stays yours.</b> On your device wherever it can be, synced privately through your own iCloud. Never sold. Ever.</div>
      <div><b>Answered by a person.</b> You email us, a person reads it and replies — no ticket queue, no bot, no runaround.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="signal" id="why" style="padding:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="reveal-h">Most apps are wired to extract. Ours are wired to help.</h2>
    <a class="em" href="#contact">Same brain. Better wiring.</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="contact" id="contact">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rule" style="justify-content:center"><span>Say hello</span></div>
    <h2 style="text-align:center;margin-inline:auto">Got a question, an idea, or a bug to report?</h2>
    <p class="sub" style="text-align:center">A person reads every message and replies. No ticket queue, no bot.</p>
    <a class="say" href="mailto:hello@neurotrocity.com">hello@neurotrocity.com</a>
  </div>
</section>

